22:25:36 | INFO | 🤖 Target: It is fair to be skeptical of the fantasy of spotless, temptation-free politicians. Most political careers involve constant contact with donors, party figures, lobbyists, advocacy groups, and people seeking access. Even without illegal bribery, that environment can normalize favors, exclusivity, and dependency. The realistic goal is not to find mythical “perfectly clean” people. It is to demand officials who make conflicts visible, decline improper benefits, do not sell access or outcomes, and accept enforcement when they cross lines. A politician can make mistakes or operate in an imperfect system without being beyond redemption—but they should not be excused for treating public office as a private asset. For your cousin, she should assume she will be offered gray-area opportunities and social pressure, not imagine she will simply avoid temptation. Her integrity will show in how she handles those moments, especially when doing the right thing costs her money, relationships, or advancement.
