22:26:48 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Local politics can be especially vulnerable because zoning, permits, land use, and construction contracts can create large private gains from a small number of decisions. The same officials may also have close personal or business ties to developers, contractors, and community power brokers. In smaller communities, oversight and local journalism can be limited, which makes conflicts easier to hide. So your concern is not limited to national politics; local government can absolutely have serious corruption and favoritism risks. The practical response is to focus on concrete safeguards: public bidding, conflict-of-interest disclosures, recusal rules, open meetings and records, independent audits, transparent campaign contributions, and local reporting or citizen oversight. For your cousin, local office may be where integrity is tested most directly. She should be particularly careful around land-use decisions, procurement, gifts, family or business connections, and informal conversations with applicants.
